---
/**
 * about.astro — /about
 * Visual reference: ALG-About-Us-v1.html (VariationC, heroVariant="typo", channelLayout="side")
 * Shell: ContentShell.astro (canonical --pad-x, 1320px cap, 56px gutter)
 * Chrome: BaseLayout (via ContentShell) — canon header + mega-menu + footer
 * A2: 6 aisle cards with consumer page icons + anchor links
 * A3: no HQ/contact block, no placeholder logo, no "2009"/"EST."
 * CFG-CHROME-3: 0 year/month in body chrome
 */
import ContentShell from '../layouts/ContentShell.astro';
---
<ContentShell
  title="About Us — Archipelago Lighting Group"
  description="Archipelago Lighting Group — OEM and white-label lighting manufacturer since 1997. Retail shelf programs and commercial & industrial spec-grade catalog through authorized channels."
  bodyClass="page-about"
>

<!-- ============================================================
     §01 HERO — typographic variant
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="block hero hero-typo" id="top">
  <div class="eyebrow">ABOUT · ARCHIPELAGO LIGHTING GROUP · MONTCLAIR, CA · SINCE 1997</div>
  <h1 class="hero-headline-big">
    Lighting,<br>
    <span class="hero-light">reinvented.</span>
  </h1>
  <p class="hero-sub">
    Built for 40-foot warehouses, K-12 corridors, cold-storage rooms,<br>
    and spec-grade projects, and the retail aisles of nine national retailers.
  </p>
  <div class="hero-meta-strip">
    <div class="hero-meta-cell"><div class="v">1997</div><div class="k">Founded</div></div>
    <div class="hero-meta-cell"><div class="v">30+ yr</div><div class="k">Supplying Shelves</div></div>
    <div class="hero-meta-cell"><div class="v">85M+</div><div class="k">Units Shipped</div></div>
    <div class="hero-meta-cell"><div class="v">9</div><div class="k">National Retail Accounts</div></div>
    <div class="hero-meta-cell"><div class="v">5</div><div class="k">US Warehouses</div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     §02 HERITAGE — story + OEM capabilities card
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="block" id="heritage">
  <div class="section-head">
    <div class="section-head-meta">
      <span class="section-num">01</span>
      <span class="section-rule"></span>
      <span class="section-label">HERITAGE · SINCE 1997</span>
    </div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Three decades of OEM discipline.</h2>
    <p class="section-kicker">From the retail shelf to the spec package — one quality system, two doors.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="heritage-grid">
    <div class="heritage-main">
      <p class="heritage-lede">
        ALG was founded in 1997 as an OEM and white-label manufacturer. For three decades we've been <em>vetted, audited, and approved</em> to put product on the shelves of America's largest home and garden retailers — The Home Depot, Lowe's, Costco, Walmart, Tractor Supply, Canadian Tire, Kroger, Fred Meyer, and Batteries Plus.
      </p>
      <p class="heritage-body-text">
        That vetting is not casual. National retailers require multi-year compliance histories, safety-listing discipline, quarterly factory audits, retail-grade packaging, and the operational maturity to refill a planogram in a single replenishment cycle. We earned a place on those shelves the long way — one passed audit, one warranty cycle, one accepted line review at a time.
      </p>
      <p class="heritage-body-text">
        Out of that retail OEM discipline grew our commercial &amp; industrial catalog. Same factories. Same quality system. <strong>A completely separate sales motion, a separate price book, and a separate set of customers.</strong> Specifiers, electrical contractors, ESCOs, EPCs, and authorized distributors never see a retail SKU in a project package — and a retail buyer never sees a spec-grade quote.
      </p>
      <div class="heritage-pull">
        <div class="heritage-pull-label">THE DISCIPLINE</div>
        <div class="heritage-pull-text">House brand, co-brand, or OEM — retail product is built to a retailer's planogram, packaging standard, and replenishment rhythm. Commercial &amp; industrial product is built to a specifier's photometric file. Neither program crosses into the other channel's aisle.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="heritage-side">
      <div class="heritage-side-card">
        <div class="heritage-side-card-head">RETAIL OEM CAPABILITIES · ACTIVE</div>
        <ul class="heritage-side-list">
          <li><span class="dot"></span><span><strong>House brand</strong> · Full private-label SKU programs under the retailer's name and UPC</span></li>
          <li><span class="dot"></span><span><strong>Co-brand</strong> · Joint program with retailer + manufacturer marks</span></li>
          <li><span class="dot"></span><span><strong>OEM / white-label</strong> · Build-to-spec for the retailer's category architecture</span></li>
          <li><span class="dot"></span><span><strong>Replenishment readiness</strong> · 5 US warehouses · same-week refill on in-season SKUs</span></li>
          <li><span class="dot"></span><span><strong>Compliance discipline</strong> · UL / ETL where applicable · outdoor IP ratings · retail warranty programs</span></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="heritage-side-footnote">Retailer-specific program documentation available under MNDA to qualified buyers.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="heritage-stat-grid">
        <div class="stat"><div class="v">30+ yr</div><div class="k">Continuous OEM operation since 1997</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="v">85M+</div><div class="k">Units shipped through retail channel</div></div>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     §03 BY THE NUMBERS — dark block
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="block block-dark" id="numbers">
  <div class="block-dark-head">
    <div class="block-dark-eyebrow">02 · BY THE NUMBERS</div>
    <div class="block-dark-title">A spec-grade manufacturer, sized for both shelves.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="numbers-grid">
    <div class="number-cell"><div class="number-v">1997</div><div class="number-k">Year founded · Montclair, CA</div></div>
    <div class="number-cell"><div class="number-v">85M+</div><div class="number-k">Units shipped through retail channel</div></div>
    <div class="number-cell"><div class="number-v">9</div><div class="number-k">National retail accounts · active</div></div>
    <div class="number-cell"><div class="number-v">6</div><div class="number-k">Retail aisles · Home to Party</div></div>
    <div class="number-cell"><div class="number-v">5</div><div class="number-k">US replenishment warehouses</div></div>
    <div class="number-cell"><div class="number-v">9</div><div class="number-k">Commercial &amp; industrial brand families</div></div>
    <div class="number-cell"><div class="number-v">8</div><div class="number-k">Industry verticals served · spec channel</div></div>
    <div class="number-cell"><div class="number-v">0</div><div class="number-k">Channel-conflict incidents · by policy</div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     §04 TWO CHANNELS — side-by-side cards
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="block" id="channels">
  <div class="section-head">
    <div class="section-head-meta">
      <span class="section-num">03</span>
      <span class="section-rule"></span>
      <span class="section-label">THE TWO CHANNELS</span>
    </div>
    <h2 class="section-title">One catalog. Two doors.</h2>
    <p class="section-kicker">ALG sells through two channels that never share a shelf, never share a part number, and never share a price sheet.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="channel-grid">
    <!-- Retail channel card -->
    <div class="channel-card ch-retail channel-card-side">
      <div class="channel-card-head">
        <div class="channel-eyebrow">RETAIL · OEM · WHITE-LABEL</div>
        <h3 class="channel-title">Retail · Consumer</h3>
        <p class="channel-tagline">On the shelves of the people who sell to consumers.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="channel-spec">
        <div class="cs-row"><dt>BUYER</dt><dd>National big-box retailers, regional chains, category managers, retail buyers</dd></div>
        <div class="cs-row"><dt>PROGRAMS</dt><dd>
          <span class="brand-chip">House brand</span>
          <span class="brand-chip">Co-brand</span>
          <span class="brand-chip">OEM / white-label</span>
          <span class="brand-chip">PolyGrow (horticultural)</span>
        </dd></div>
        <div class="cs-row"><dt>DISTRIBUTION</dt><dd>The Home Depot · Lowe's · Costco · Walmart · Tractor Supply · Canadian Tire · Kroger · Fred Meyer · Batteries Plus</dd></div>
        <div class="cs-row"><dt>SCALE</dt><dd>6 retail aisles · UPC + PDQ + shelf-ready packaging · planogram-mapped</dd></div>
        <div class="cs-row"><dt>WARRANTY</dt><dd>Retail-program warranty · built for replenishment economics</dd></div>
        <div class="cs-row"><dt>PRICING</dt><dd>Retailer-set · we never set consumer price</dd></div>
        <div class="cs-row"><dt>LEAD TIME</dt><dd>5 US warehouses · same-week replenishment on in-season SKUs</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <div class="channel-note">
        <span class="channel-note-label">CHANNEL POLICY</span>
        <span class="channel-note-text">ALG does not sell directly to consumers. Every retail SKU ships through a vetted retailer.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="channel-cta-row">
        <a href="/contact?topic=retail" class="btn-primary">Become a retail buyer →</a>
        <a href="/contact?topic=oem" class="btn-ghost">Request capability deck</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <!-- C&I channel card -->
    <div class="channel-card ch-ci channel-card-side">
      <div class="channel-card-head">
        <div class="channel-eyebrow">COMMERCIAL &amp; INDUSTRIAL · SPEC-GRADE</div>
        <h3 class="channel-title">Commercial &amp; Industrial</h3>
        <p class="channel-tagline">Specified, quoted, and installed through authorized channels only.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="channel-spec">
        <div class="cs-row"><dt>BUYER</dt><dd>Specifiers, electrical contractors, ESCOs, EPCs, lighting agents, authorized distributors</dd></div>
        <div class="cs-row"><dt>BRAND FAMILIES</dt><dd>
          <span class="brand-chip">plano<span class="aa">Ⓐ</span>RCH</span>
          <span class="brand-chip">lampar<span class="aa">Ⓐ</span>RCH</span>
          <span class="brand-chip">lux<span class="aa">Ⓐ</span>RCH</span>
          <span class="brand-chip">city<span class="aa">Ⓐ</span>RCH</span>
          <span class="brand-chip">multi-f<span class="aa">Ⓐ</span>MILY</span>
          <span class="brand-chip">tubul<span class="aa">Ⓐ</span>RCH</span>
          <span class="brand-chip">sign<span class="aa">Ⓐ</span>TURE</span>
          <span class="brand-chip">const<span class="aa">Ⓐ</span>NT</span>
          <span class="brand-chip">contr<span class="aa">Ⓐ</span>LS</span>
        </dd></div>
        <div class="cs-row"><dt>DISTRIBUTION</dt><dd>Authorized distributors · independent reps (AURA portal) · ALG distributor portal · direct project quote</dd></div>
        <div class="cs-row"><dt>SCALE</dt><dd>8 industry verticals · DLC Premium / Standard · LM-79 + LM-80 photometric library on file</dd></div>
        <div class="cs-row"><dt>WARRANTY</dt><dd>5–10 yr by tier · ECO · PRO · PRO+</dd></div>
        <div class="cs-row"><dt>PRICING</dt><dd>Quote · project · rebate-eligible · TAA-compliant SKUs available</dd></div>
        <div class="cs-row"><dt>LEAD TIME</dt><dd>Hundreds of thousands of units available to ship from US stock</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <div class="channel-note">
        <span class="channel-note-label">CHANNEL POLICY</span>
        <span class="channel-note-text">C&amp;I product is never sold through retail aisles. Authorized distribution only.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="channel-cta-row">
        <a href="/contact?topic=spec" class="btn-primary">Talk to a spec rep →</a>
        <a href="/find-a-distributor/" class="btn-ghost">Find a distributor</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <!-- Channel rule bar -->
  <div class="channel-rule-bar">
    <div class="channel-rule-bar-label">HOW WE KEEP THE TWO CHANNELS HONEST</div>
    <p class="channel-rule-intro">A retailer's shelf is valuable real estate; a specifier's project package is a contract. Both depend on trust that our product only shows up where it's supposed to. We protect that trust with five written rules.</p>
    <ul class="channel-rule-list">
      <li><span class="rl-n">01</span><span><strong>Retail product is sold only by retailers.</strong> ALG does not list retail SKUs on its own commercial-facing site, in its distributor portal, or in any project quote. Consumers buy from our retail partners — not from us.</span></li>
      <li><span class="rl-n">02</span><span><strong>Commercial &amp; industrial product is sold only through authorized channels.</strong> plano<span class="aa">Ⓐ</span>RCH, lampar<span class="aa">Ⓐ</span>RCH, lux<span class="aa">Ⓐ</span>RCH and the rest of the C&amp;I families ship only via authorized distributors, reps, and the ALG distributor portal — never via retail aisles or direct consumer e-commerce.</span></li>
      <li><span class="rl-n">03</span><span><strong>No SKU lives in both channels.</strong> Form factors may rhyme — a retail garage light and a commercial high-bay share a driver platform — but the SKU number, the UPC, the listing, and the warranty are channel-specific.</span></li>
      <li><span class="rl-n">04</span><span><strong>Separate sales orgs, separate price books.</strong> Retail account managers do not quote projects. Spec reps do not negotiate planograms. Pricing for each channel is built against that channel's cost stack and never reconciled in the field.</span></li>
      <li><span class="rl-n">05</span><span><strong>Shared everything else.</strong> Same factory floor, same driver bench, same QA log, same warranty rigor. A failure learned on a retail SKU patches a spec SKU, and vice versa.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
